                <invention-title lang="de">MEHRBAND-ANTENNENANORDNUNG MIT ZIRKULARER POLARISATION</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">DISPOSITION D'ANTENNE À POLARISATION CIRCULAIRE MULTIBANDE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">MULTIBAND CIRCULAR POLARIZED ANTENNA ARRANGEMENT</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A circularly polarized, multiband, and wideband antenna and can communicate with a GPS system. Comprising an antenna assembly 100, a communication assembly 101 comprising a sensor transmission unit 105 communicatively connected to an acoustic sensor 110, and the antenna assembly 100. A pit lid 115 wherein the antenna assembly 100 is mechanically coupled to the pit lid 115 and positioned between the pit lid and a pipe 125. The acoustic sensor 110 is physically coupled to a valve stem 121 within a valve chamber 120. The antenna may include a driving element, first, second and third conductive parasitic elements electrically connected to the driving element, and a ground plane. The parasitic elements are provided with different lengths to provide for wider band operation with multiple resonant frequencies. The radiated wave has a low angle of propagation and travels for at least 1-2 miles.</p>
            </abstract>
